<title>UK: ALGERIA SAYS PUMPED 802,000 BPD IN JULY.</title>
<headline>ALGERIA SAYS PUMPED 802,000 BPD IN JULY.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria told OPEC on Thursday it pumped 802,000 barrels a day (bpd) of crude in July, 52,000 bpd over its official OPEC quota.</p>
<p>Algeria submitted the data to OPEC secretariat headquarters in Vienna, the OPEC news agency reported.</p>
<p>Production and supply data for July according to member country submissions to the OPEC Secretariat so far were as follows (in million bpd):</p>
<p>			Production	 Supply</p>
<p>     Algeria	  0.802	    0.800</p>
<p>Indonesia</p>
<p>Iran</p>
<p>Iraq</p>
<p>     Kuwait	   2.0081</p>
<p>Libya</p>
<p>Nigeria</p>
<p>     Qatar	    0.3912	   0.3571</p>
<p>     Saudi Arabia   8.0003	   8.0007</p>
<p>UAE</p>
<p>     Venezuela	2.413</p>
<p>Supply as defined by OPEC is calculated as domestic consumption plus net export sales of crude and products, plus withdrawals of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
</text>
